  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The legal proceedings against Paul Mackenzie concern the Shakahola forest deaths, a mass casualty event involving a doomsday cult in Kenya. Investigations into the cult revealed that followers were coerced into starvation under the direction of Mackenzie. Earlier in November 2026, Mackenzie received a 200-year prison sentence following his conviction for the murder of 190 children. Recent court rulings by Justice Alex Ithuku have expanded the scope of his criminal culpability, establishing his involvement in the deaths of 123 additional victims between 2021 and 2023. While he faced multiple counts, the court acquitted him regarding a separate group of 115 deaths. The case highlights ongoing efforts by the Kenyan judiciary to hold cult leadership accountable for the organized harm inflicted upon members within the Shakahola sect.",
